some new ideas so that you can

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:32.370
trend your life in a better direction.

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:36.810
Okay, so a microcosm is
defined as a community, place,

00:00:36.810 --> 00:00:41.160
or situation regarded as
encapsulating in miniature

00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:44.280
the characteristic qualities or features

00:00:44.280 --> 00:00:45.990
of something much larger.

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:49.380
Feel free to pause the video
and really soak that in,

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.740
and while you're soaking that
in, let me ask you a question.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:56.220
What's the difference
between life and living?

00:00:56.220 --> 00:01:00.330
You know, life itself may seem
like a simple enough concept

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:02.850
because we talk about it all the time.

00:01:02.850 --> 00:01:05.370
I have a life, you have a life.

00:01:05.370 --> 00:01:09.180
It's the thing we are all a
part of and all seem to have.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.200
But if I ask you to
describe what your life is,

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:15.510
it's a little bit more difficult to do so

00:01:15.510 --> 00:01:18.270
because there's so much involved in life

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:21.450
and your life is kind of just everything

00:01:21.450 --> 00:01:23.130
that has to do with you.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:25.740
Your family situation growing up,

00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.870
your family situation right now,

00:01:27.870 --> 00:01:30.120
it might be the job that you have,

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:32.340
the job that you want to have,

00:01:32.340 --> 00:01:34.440
your hopes and dreams for the future,

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.110
your trauma and regret of the past,

00:01:37.110 --> 00:01:39.870
every idea that bounces around your skull

00:01:39.870 --> 00:01:42.300
or has bounced around in your skull.

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:47.010
Life is everything, and since
it describes everything,

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:50.250
it also kind of describes
nothing in particular.

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:53.700
It's an all encompassing
idea that is basically

00:01:53.700 --> 00:01:56.010
just a theme and a concept,

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.960
something we're all familiar with

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:00.660
but none of us truly understand.

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:04.800
Living on the other hand is
something that we experience,

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:07.620
something that you are doing right now.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:10.350
Living is something you've always done

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:14.220
and something you always
will do because by definition

00:02:14.220 --> 00:02:17.640
before you were living
was before you were you,

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:20.880
and when you stop living,
you will stop being you,

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:24.300
so you and living are the same thing.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.820
You don't know what it's like to not live.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:30.270
In some ways though,
your life and your living

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.950
are not unlike each other.

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:35.430
They both deal with similar
people, places and things.

00:02:35.430 --> 00:02:37.950
They both have familiar faces,

00:02:37.950 --> 00:02:39.870
people you know and love

00:02:39.870 --> 00:02:43.050
or strongly dislike and want to avoid.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:47.310
Both have dealt and will
deal with similar emotions,

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:51.900
similar feelings, tendencies,
actions, and reactions,

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:55.860
but despite their commonalities,
one remains a stranger,

00:02:55.860 --> 00:02:58.920
something we can only look
at through abstraction,

00:02:58.920 --> 00:03:02.490
through memories we recall but can't see,

00:03:02.490 --> 00:03:05.670
and places we'll go but never be,

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:09.090
because no matter how much
we think about our life,

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:11.820
it will never make sense to us completely.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:15.324
It's impossible to see it all at once.

00:03:15.324 --> 00:03:18.120
It's impossible to grasp what our life is.

00:03:18.120 --> 00:03:22.350
We only see fragments
and patterns and themes

00:03:22.350 --> 00:03:25.800
and in a lot of ways,
that's exactly what life is.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:28.860
It's a pattern of
moments, strung together.

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:33.060
It's the overarching theme
of decisions that we've made

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:36.120
in days like today, so
if we take a step back

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.790
and we think about our entire life

00:03:38.790 --> 00:03:41.220
and we don't like what we see,

00:03:41.220 --> 00:03:44.220
we're basically saying we
don't like the pattern,

00:03:44.220 --> 00:03:45.930
we don't like the theme.

00:03:45.930 --> 00:03:48.420
If life is everything all at once

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:51.120
and living is the day to day,

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:56.010
then by definition, each
day is a microcosm of life.

00:03:56.010 --> 00:03:58.890
Each day we live is a situation

00:03:58.890 --> 00:04:01.200
that encapsulates in miniature

00:04:01.200 --> 00:04:05.040
the characteristic qualities
or features of our life,

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:08.040
and when we start to realize
this, we'll start to realize

00:04:08.040 --> 00:04:12.090
that life isn't really
something we can interact with.

00:04:12.090 --> 00:04:15.690
We don't have access to our life.

00:04:15.690 --> 00:04:18.960
The only thing that we
have access to is living,

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:23.070
playing it out day by
day, decision by decision,

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:27.360
and our tendencies and our
impulses to do certain things

00:04:27.360 --> 00:04:30.930
are essentially the only
thing that we can influence

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:33.450
when it comes to our existence.

00:04:33.450 --> 00:04:34.590
So what does this all mean?

00:04:34.590 --> 00:04:37.680
Well, it means that if
you survey your life,

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:39.810
you look at the direction
that you're heading,

00:04:39.810 --> 00:04:41.970
you look at the things that you dislike

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:44.250
about your life and about yourself.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:45.930
Maybe you don't like the fact

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:49.260
that you never have the
motivation to go to the gym

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:51.720
or you can't seem to focus at work,

00:04:51.720 --> 00:04:53.790
and it leads to poor job performance

00:04:53.790 --> 00:04:55.320
which leads to less money,

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.600
which means that you can't
put food on the table.

00:04:57.600 --> 00:04:59.880
Maybe you're not proud of who you are.

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:01.740
Maybe you don't take care of yourself.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.320
Maybe you have serious feelings of regret

00:05:04.320 --> 00:05:07.530
about things you did or
didn't do in the past.

00:05:07.530 --> 00:05:10.740
Maybe you have wild
uncertainty about the future

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:14.370
or you're fairly convinced that
there is no future for you.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:18.510
Well, these things are all life things,

00:05:18.510 --> 00:05:21.210
but you don't experience life.

00:05:21.210 --> 00:05:22.620
You experience living.

00:05:22.620 --> 00:05:26.970
Living is confined by
constant beginnings and ends,

00:05:26.970 --> 00:05:31.020
sunrise, sunset, again
and again and again.

00:05:31.020 --> 00:05:34.230
You are living right now and
it's all you've been doing,

00:05:34.230 --> 00:05:37.110
so if there are things that
you don't like about your life

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:39.690
then the only thing you
can do to change them

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:42.780
is to change the way you live today.

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.760
Maybe you're thinking
I need to quit smoking,

00:05:44.760 --> 00:05:48.690
and one day I'm gonna quit
smoking for the rest of my life,

00:05:48.690 --> 00:05:50.160
and I'm gonna live the rest of my life

00:05:50.160 --> 00:05:51.870
free from this nasty habit,

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.350
and I'm gonna be happy and
healthy all the live long day

00:05:55.350 --> 00:05:58.320
as if that's somehow different
than not smoking today,

00:05:58.320 --> 00:05:59.610
'cause each time we wake up,

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:01.290
we're confronted with an opportunity

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:06.030
to echo the familiar motif
that's become the central theme,

00:06:06.030 --> 00:06:08.820
or we can realize that our entire life

00:06:08.820 --> 00:06:11.700
